PATCH 410: thread the DROPPED c60a/c61a args in FUN_1000_a547 (the in-mission "range/status" cockpit-HUD
element), asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x1a577-0x1a58a.  Fixes the in-mission render CRAWL
(the "hangs after a short time" symptom).

THE BUG (in-mission ~2.5fps crawl -> reads as a hang).  Profiling the browser mission paint chain
(459a -> 206f -> 209e dirty-walk -> handler 0x77dc=795c -> 78ca cockpit-status HUD) isolated ~100% of the
frame wallclock to FUN_1000_a547's FIRST call: `(*c60a)()` == 373-1130ms per call.  DGROUP:0x60a is the
MGAVIDEO SOLID rect-fill FUN_0000_1091 (bx=rect near-offset, al=color).  The asm (0x1a577) is:
  1a577 mov al,0x50 ; 1a579 mov bx,0x967c ; 1a57c call [0x60a]   (then 1a584 mov bx,0x967c; 1a587 call [0x61a])
Ghidra dropped BOTH args -> 1091 read a GARBAGE bx (undefined register) as the rect near-offset and filled
a WILD, near-screen-size rect (0.4-1.1s per fill) EVERY frame the HUD element painted -> the crawl.  (The
voxel terrain df0e->9200 is 1ms; audio pump 0ms -- a547/1091 was the entire cost.)

FIX.  Thread bx=0x967c (the rect descriptor DGROUP near-offset = &DAT_2000_567c, whose [y0,x0,y1,x1] fields
a547 itself just wrote: 967c=param_1, 9680=param_1+9, 9675/967a from the vehicle) and al=0x50 (color) into
the c60a call; thread bx=0x967c into the c61a call (asm 0x1a584-0x1a587).  c60a signature (undefined2 bx,
undefined1 al) is the SAME cast patch 305 (fist:60409) uses for the sibling HUD 1091 call.  With the real
rect, 1091 fills the intended small status box (rows = y1-y0 = 9) instead of a wild one.

VERIFIED.  Build instantiates + runs (node menu = NovaLogic banner + framebuffer); native<->wasm(node)
BYTE-IDENTICAL on mainmenu AND mission-cockpit (AZER1/SAUDI1/AZER2) DIFF=0 -- byte-neutral on the whole
covered matrix (a547 is reached only by the 459a in-mission live paint, unreached by the frozen-capture
verify flows, so it cannot regress any verified frame).  The in-mission crawl-elimination is asm-reasoned +
measured at the source (c60a was 373-1130ms on garbage bx; the real rect y0=0x14/y1=0x1d bounds it to 9
rows); direct browser-in-mission observation was blocked this round by headless-chromium .data-preload
flakiness (a harness gap, not the fix).  board:0001

